#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:5
#: bb31f9118cde47169947336db2e010d3
msgid "Spektrum RC Systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:7
#: 38a7a28d39eb4647b79bcd1d53c2f05d
msgid "Any DSM/DSM2 compatible receiver can be used with ArduPilot. Spektrum also makes receivers with SBus, PPM, SRXL and SXRL2 protocols which are also compatible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:9
#: 247d17465b1e4e57bea853c6957173bc
msgid "For a **Spektrum DSM**, **DSM2**, or **DSM-X Satellite** receiver, connect to the **SPKT/DSM** port (some boards, such as the CUBE mini carrier board, require you to modify solder bridges. See the autopilot board's documentation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:16
#: dab61e0cddc1422cbe2d503694c140e0
msgid "Spektrum Satellite Receivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:18
#: d15e9c31c94244dea36b280e9e9dc374
msgid "`Spektrum Satellite Receivers <http://www.spektrumrc.com/Products/Default.aspx?ProdID=SPM9645>`__ work as a DSM receiver with Pixhawk. Spektrum satellite receivers do not have buttons to bind, so there are two ways to bind them to a transmitter. They are connected as if they were PPM-SUM or SBus output devices. ArduPilot automatically discovers the serial protocol being used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:23
#: 9c70266d3b99400193ab9cd753a90def
msgid "Pre-bind the Spektrum Satellite to your transmitter using a conventional Spektrum receiver with satellite attached, then disconnect the satellite from the conventional receiver, and connect it to the Spektrum port on autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:27
#: a679b0b9acdc4c14977610e3852b0f24
msgid "Bind the satellite receiver using Mission Planner to initiate the bind. This functionality is located in Radio Calibration screen on Initial Setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:34
#: 78cf052b4e644e9d8fbaefdc11b80493
msgid "Being a satellite, range may be limited and the preceding receivers and methods may provide greater range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:46
#: 73b85f7f241f4d79b45c0b9f595a4770
msgid "Spektrum SRXL2 Receivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:48
#: 5374fc81f4c346ecbfc11ad3c75e9a16
msgid "All Spektrum receivers released since August 2019 only support the `SRXL2 <https://github.com/SpektrumRC/SRXL2>`__ protocol. SRXL2 is a single-wire, half-duplex protocol that supports integrated telemetry and a number of other features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:50
#: 78af7d4af7bf4a229c431bf1c5692b99
msgid "An `SRXL2 cable <https://www.spektrumrc.com/Products/Default.aspx?ProdID=SPM4650>`__ has four wires, one of which is not connected. This new format is to distinguish them from older receivers supporting DSMX since DSMX and SRXL2 are incompatible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:52
#: 86448e5acdd24d8e87fc973431343293
msgid "SRXL2 receivers must be connected to a UART. SRXL2 receivers support a wide range of voltages, including the 5v available on a UART so connect GND to GND, VCC  to VCC and the signal wire to the TX pin of the UART."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:54
#: 8873c825758e489b8229810fe9e0fde0
msgid "In the configuration of the serial port select the RCIN protocol and set the serial options to half-duplex operation. So for example for serial port 4:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:56
#: 5e32c790200644da9fad588e23db03fa
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL4_PROTOCOL <SERIAL4_PROTOCOL>` = 23"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:57
#: 755d3d086b7e4e708eaf55e77c26d561
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL4_OPTIONS <SERIAL4_OPTIONS>` = 4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:58
#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:64
#: c72c7518c5064cd3bec92fd4250cc3d0
#: 9479682c8a5940e8b552208d9c8bec21
msgid "Set :ref:`RSSI_TYPE <RSSI_TYPE>` = 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:60
#: 6ec1d61d46414abd8f8582bf9d13476a
msgid "Many single board autopilots support RC input on serial port 6 only exposing the RX connection. For F7 autopilots, such as the Kakute F7, it is necessary to swap the RX and TX pins in order to support SRXL2. It is also necessary to support serial access on the UART by using the board's alternate configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:62
#: 4fd68acd290946eb869d3933ae8dd715
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL6_PROTOCOL <SERIAL6_PROTOCOL>` = 23"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:63
#: 0d2224e3edd741f3a23e482ab2790282
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL6_OPTIONS <SERIAL6_OPTIONS>` = 12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:65
#: 88867339352645138fc497ac08e49313
msgid "Set :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG <BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spektrum-rc.rst:67
#: c905a9896c554284aa4e95256d50a9db
msgid "With the receiver connected and configured correctly proceed with RC calibration as normal."
msgstr ""
